 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-08",
  "asof": "2026-09-09 09:27 UTC",
  "headline": "Dealer gamma flipped negative \u2014 and the heat figure in yesterday's brief was wrong",
  "standfirst": "One real change and one correction. Net gamma went from +$36.13B to \u2212$3.98B, so dealer hedging now amplifies moves rather than damping them, with spot sitting 0.04% from the flip \u2014 on it, not near it. The correction is the book: this brief reported heat of 7.19R yesterday and called it 2.4 times the cap. That number pools both accounts and divides by one account's capital. Recomputed with the engine's own formula, your heat is 4.04R against a 3.0R cap \u2014 over it, but by a hair, and no position size or stop has changed since August. Underneath, the 2s10s curve flattened to 44bp, the yen rallied 3.87% on the week with the BoJ 97% priced to hike, and crude closed +20.56% on the month with CPI two sessions away.",
  "themes": [],
  "ondeck": "Apple's product event is today, Wednesday 9 September; August CPI lands Friday 11 September at 08:30 ET and is the regime's tightest gate; the Bank of Japan meets next week with a hike 97%% priced; the FOMC meets 15\u201316 September; triple witching is 18 September.",
  "note": null
